{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.FluidDynamics.qou_ns_in_qou","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.qou_ns_in_qou","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Ring.Defs","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.NormNum"],"declarations":15,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.descartes_internal_ns_singular","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.descartes_internal_ns_singular","kind":"theorem","line":156,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FluidDynamics/qou_ns_in_qou.lean#L156-L162","doc":"**The Descartes QOU's internal q-NS is singular — unconditionally.** The\ncapstone applied to the concrete instance; no `sorry`, no open hypothesis\n(still an *in-QOU* statement, not the `ℝ³` PDE). Witnesses that the general\n`qou_internal_ns_singular` is not vacuous. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.descartesQOU","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.descartesQOU","kind":"def","line":141,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FluidDynamics/qou_ns_in_qou.lean#L141-L154","doc":"**The Descartes QOU** (`χ(A) = -6`, Bring's surface; `ns-singularity-descartes`)\nas a concrete `QOUFluidUniverse ℤ`. The obstruction is the global class\n`e(ξ) ∈ H²(S, ℤ) ≅ ℤ`, modelled by its degree `-6 = χ(A)` and `internalBlowup` is *defined* as `NS(A) ≠ 0` (the categorical\nmeaning of NS-singular). Every base field discharges sorry-free: `-6 ≠ 0` is\ndecidable arithmetic, and Step 3 is `Iff.rfl`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.qou_not_internally_regular","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.qou_not_internally_regular","kind":"theorem","line":132,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FluidDynamics/qou_ns_in_qou.lean#L132-L137","doc":"**Contrapositive scope check.** If a QOU's internal q-NS flow were regular,\nits NS obstruction would vanish — impossible for a genuine QOU. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.qou_internal_ns_singular","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.qou_internal_ns_singular","kind":"theorem","line":122,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FluidDynamics/qou_ns_in_qou.lean#L122-L130","doc":"**Given a QOU, its internal q-NS flow at `q = 1` is singular.**\n\nDerived by composing the QOU's own structural steps: observability ⇒\n`χ(A) ≠ 0` ⇒ `e(ξ) ≠ 0` in `H²(S)` ⇒ internal blow-up. A statement **about the QOU** —\nit does **not** resolve the classical Navier–Stokes problem, and\n`internalBlowup` is the categorical internal observable, not the `ℝ³` PDE. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.qou_obstruction_nonzero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.qou_obstruction_nonzero","kind":"theorem","line":116,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FluidDynamics/qou_ns_in_qou.lean#L116-L120","doc":"**The QOU's NS obstruction is nonzero.** Given a QOU, the global class\n`NS(A) = e(ξ) ≠ 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.QOUFluidUniverse.obstruction_iff_internal_blowup","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.QOUFluidUniverse.obstruction_iff_internal_blowup","kind":"theorem","line":112,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FluidDynamics/qou_ns_in_qou.lean#L112-L112","doc":"**Step 3 (`ns-obstruction`):** a nonzero NS obstruction *is*, by\ndefinition, the QOU's internal q-NS singularity (NS-singular ⟺ NS(A)≠0). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.QOUFluidUniverse.chi_forces_obstruction","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.QOUFluidUniverse.chi_forces_obstruction","kind":"theorem","line":109,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FluidDynamics/qou_ns_in_qou.lean#L109-L109","doc":"**Step 2 (item 1 of `thm:ns-singularity-descartes`):** `deg e(ξ) = χ(A)`,\nso `χ(A) ≠ 0` forces the global class `NS(A) ≠ 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.QOUFluidUniverse.observability_forces_chi","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.QOUFluidUniverse.observability_forces_chi","kind":"theorem","line":106,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FluidDynamics/qou_ns_in_qou.lean#L106-L106","doc":"**Step 1 (`qou-obstruction-reduction`):** observability forces `χ(A) ≠ 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.QOUFluidUniverse.internalBlowup","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.QOUFluidUniverse.internalBlowup","kind":"def","line":104,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FluidDynamics/qou_ns_in_qou.lean#L104-L104","doc":"\"The QOU's internal q-NS flow at `q = 1` is singular\" — categorical\ninternal observable (`blowup-yekutieli`), NOT the `ℝ³` PDE. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.QOUFluidUniverse.obstruction","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.QOUFluidUniverse.obstruction","kind":"def","line":101,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FluidDynamics/qou_ns_in_qou.lean#L101-L101","doc":"The NS obstruction `NS(A) := e(ξ)`, the **global** Euler class of the Reeb\nbundle in `H²(S, ℤ) ≅ ℤ` (not its restriction to `Σ`, which is always 0). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.QOUFluidUniverse.eulerChar","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.QOUFluidUniverse.eulerChar","kind":"def","line":98,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FluidDynamics/qou_ns_in_qou.lean#L98-L98","doc":"The Euler characteristic `χ(A) : ℤ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.QOUFluidUniverse.observability_holds","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.QOUFluidUniverse.observability_holds","kind":"theorem","line":96,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FluidDynamics/qou_ns_in_qou.lean#L96-L96","doc":"A QOU satisfies its observability axiom by definition. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.QOUFluidUniverse.observability","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.QOUFluidUniverse.observability","kind":"def","line":94,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FluidDynamics/qou_ns_in_qou.lean#L94-L94","doc":"**Observability axiom**: `Hom_𝐂(𝟙, Ad(A)) = 0` (condition (ii) of\n`def:quantum-observable-universe`). Held by definition of a QOU. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.QOUFluidUniverse.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.QOUFluidUniverse.mk","kind":"ctor","line":91,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FluidDynamics/qou_ns_in_qou.lean#L91-L91","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.QOUFluidUniverse","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.QOUFluidUniverse","kind":"structure","line":87,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FluidDynamics/qou_ns_in_qou.lean#L87-L112","doc":"The q-NS data **of a given Quantum Observable Universe** `(𝐂, A, τ)` over\n`k` — the definitional/arithmetic chain. `internalBlowup` is the QOU's\n**internal** q-NS singularity observable at `q = 1` (categorical), *not* the\nclassical `ℝ³` PDE. ","signatureChunk":0}]}